1
00:00:01,959 --> 00:00:03,467
Hello?

2
00:00:03,467 --> 00:00:09,225
Oh, hello. I wanted to enquire about hiring a room in the Village Hall,

3
00:00:09,225 --> 00:00:11,968
for the evening of September the first.

4
00:00:11,968 --> 00:00:18,800
Let me just see ... Yes, we have both rooms available that evening.

5
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:26,679
(Q1) There's our Main Hall - that's got seating for 200 people. Or there's the Charlton Room...

6
00:00:26,679 --> 00:00:27,658
Sorry?

7
00:00:27,658 --> 00:00:35,180
[Q1答案句] The Charlton Room - C-H-A-R-L-T-O-N. Charlton Room，

8
00:00:35,180 --> 00:00:38,437
That's got seating for up to one hundred.

9
00:00:38,437 --> 00:00:47,255
(Q2) Well, we're organizing a dinner to raise money for a charity, and we're hoping for at least 150 people,

10
00:00:47,255 --> 00:00:53,612
[Q2定位词] so I think well go for the Main Hall. How much would that cost?

11
00:00:53,612 --> 00:00:59,174
Let's see. You wanted it for the evening of September 1st?

12
00:00:59,174 --> 00:01:01,279
Yes, that's a Saturday.

13
00:01:01,279 --> 00:01:13,707
[Q2答案句+干扰] So from six pm to midnight that'd be 115 - that's the weekend price, it's 75 on weekdays.

14
00:01:13,707 --> 00:01:15,142
That's all right.

15
00:01:15,142 --> 00:01:20,955
(Q3) And I have to tell you there's also a deposit of 250,

16
00:01:20,955 --> 00:01:24,885
which is returnable of course as long as there's no damage.

17
00:01:24,885 --> 00:01:31,414
[Q3答案句] But we do insist that this is paid in cash, we don't take cards for that.

18
00:01:31,414 --> 00:01:39,469
You can pay the actual rent of the room however you like though - cash, credit card, cheque ...

19
00:01:39,469 --> 00:01:42,056
Oh, well I suppose that's OK.

20
00:01:42,056 --> 00:01:47,621
(Q4) So does the charge include use of tables and chairs and so on?

21
00:01:47,621 --> 00:01:49,098
oh, yes.

22
00:01:49,098 --> 00:01:51,467
[Q4答案句] And what about parking?

23
00:01:51,467 --> 00:01:59,832
Yeah, that's all included. The only thing that isn't included is...you said you were organising a dinner?

24
00:01:59,832 --> 00:02:00,869
Yeah.

25
00:02:00,869 --> 00:02:07,735
Well, you'll have to pay extra for the kitchen if you want to use that. It's 25.

26
00:02:07,735 --> 00:02:13,355
It's got very good facilities - good quality cookers and fridges and so on.

27
00:02:13,355 --> 00:02:20,284
OK, well I suppose that s all right. We can cover the cost in our entry charges.

28
00:02:20,284 --> 00:02:24,197
Right. So I'll make a note of that.

29
00:02:24,197 --> 00:02:29,548
(Q5) Now there are just one or two things you need to think about before the event.

30
00:02:29,548 --> 00:02:36,617
[Q5答案句] For example, you'll have to see about getting a licence if you're planning to have any music during the meal.

31
00:02:36,617 --> 00:02:37,730
Oh, really?

32
00:02:37,730 --> 00:02:41,961
it's quite straightforward, I'll give you the details later on.

33
00:02:41,961 --> 00:02:48,888
(Q6) And about a week or ten days before your event you'll need to contact the caretaker,

34
00:02:48,888 --> 00:02:55,207
[Q6答案句] that's Mr Evans, to make the arrangements for entry-he'll sort that out with you.

35
00:02:55,207 --> 00:02:58,146
And do I give him the payment as well?

36
00:02:58,146 --> 00:03:04,687
No, you do that directly with me.

37
00:03:04,687 --> 00:03:10,622
(Q7) Right. Now is there anything I need to know about what happens during the event?

38
00:03:10,622 --> 00:03:15,909
Well, as you'll be aware, of course the building is no smoking throughout.

39
00:03:15,909 --> 00:03:17,177
Of course.

40
00:03:17,177 --> 00:03:19,315
Now, are you having a band?

41
00:03:19,315 --> 00:03:20,510
Yes.

42
00:03:20,510 --> 00:03:22,818
Well, they'll have a lot of equipment,

43
00:03:22,818 --> 00:03:30,455
[Q7答案句] so rather than using the front door they should park their van round the back and use the stage door there.

44
00:03:30,455 --> 00:03:35,144
(Q8) You can open that from inside but don't forget to lock it at the end.

45
00:03:35,144 --> 00:03:36,456
OK.

46
00:03:36,456 --> 00:03:40,773
And talking of bands, I'm sure I don't need to tell you this,

47
00:03:40,773 --> 00:03:47,004
but you must make sure that no one fiddles about with the black box by the fire door

48
00:03:47,004 --> 00:03:54,005
that's a system that cuts in when the volume reaches a certain level. It's a legal requirement.

49
00:03:54,005 --> 00:04:01,052
Sure. Anyway, we want people to be able to talk to one another so we don't want anything too loud.

50
00:04:01,052 --> 00:04:08,415
Oh, that reminds me, we'll be having speeches - are there any microphones available?

51
00:04:08,415 --> 00:04:12,538
Yeah. Just let the caretaker know, he'll get those for you.

52
00:04:12,538 --> 00:04:19,796
[Q8定位词] Right, now when the event is over we do ask that the premises are left in good condition.

53
00:04:19,796 --> 00:04:26,086
[Q8答案句] So there's a locked cupboard and you'll be informed of the code you need to open that.

54
00:04:26,086 --> 00:04:32,157
(Q9) It's got all the cleaning equipment, brushes and detergent and so on.

55
00:04:32,157 --> 00:04:39,501
Right. So what do we need to do after everyone's gone? Sweep the floors I suppose?

56
00:04:39,501 --> 00:04:44,308
[Q9答案句] Well, actually they have to be washed, not just swept.

57
00:04:44,308 --> 00:04:48,033
(Q10) Then you'll be provided with black plastic bags,

58
00:04:48,033 --> 00:04:52,334
[Q10答案句] so all the rubbish must be collected up and left outside the door.

59
00:04:52,334 --> 00:04:56,081
Of course. We'll make sure everything's left tidy.

60
00:04:56,081 --> 00:05:02,385
Oh, and I forgot to ask, I presume we can have decorations in the room?

61
00:05:02,385 --> 00:05:05,861
Yes, but you must take them down afterwards.

62
00:05:05,861 --> 00:05:06,953
Sure.

63
00:05:06,953 --> 00:05:12,470
And the chairs and tables should be stacked up neatly at the back of the room.

64
00:05:12,470 --> 00:05:14,970
I'll make sure I've got a few people to help me.

